 ```
 One cutout at a time (about 1.5 GB of RAM). It prints a progress line every 30 seconds.
 
+**Error pass (right after the first assemble, before the cutout and before any caption or insert is timed):**
+```bash
+PY SK/scripts/find_errors.py <project> --lang es      # errors.txt + edl_tight.json
+```
+It flags PAUSA (dead air, measured against the room's own noise floor), MULETILLA (eh, este, o sea...), REPETIDA
+(doubled words, restarted phrases), DUDOSA (low-confidence words: likely mispronounced) and CORTADA (a segment edge
+that clips a syllable). Show the user the list in plain words. Apply the removable ones by copying edl_tight.json
+over edl.json and re-running assemble.py + transcribe_cut.py, then run it again until it only reports DUDOSA lines.
+DUDOSA words can't be fixed by cutting: ask the user to listen (re-record, use another take, or keep it).
+Doing this after captions/inserts exist shifts every later word time and desyncs the inserts.
+
 ### 5. Inserts in parallel (as soon as the EDL is locked)
