 - Lead-in captions centred in front of the speaker read better than lines pinned to the left edge.
 - Words behind the head are the signature move, but only when readable.
 
+## House rules (client feedback, apply to EVERY video, do not re-litigate)
+1. **Language:** the clips are in Spanish. Transcribe with the multilingual models and `language='es'` (ingest.py and
+   transcribe_cut.py already do), captions in Spanish, report to the user in simple Spanish.
+2. **Error pass first:** run `find_errors.py` right after the first assemble and cut every PAUSA / MULETILLA /
+   REPETIDA before timing any caption or insert. Show DUDOSA words to the user. If a pause cut leaves a sliver
+   shorter than ~0.5s, merge it into the neighbouring shot instead of making a flash cut.
+3. **Motion graphics that explain what is said:** every key idea gets an animated insert that illustrates it
+   (numbers, results, the problem crossed out, the offer, the CTA). Also reference what is physically in the shot:
+   props, the setting, the metaphor he uses (a chessboard -> a chess move on "movimiento/avanzar", a king falling on
+   "jaque mate"). Build them with parallel sub-agents (overlays.md). Remotion is also installed in
+   the `remotion/` folder of the editor-reels-ia repo for complex ones (free only for teams of up to 3 people).
+4. **Two typefaces per video, no more:** 'Inter Tight' (all sans: captions, tracked caps, UI inside inserts) +
+   'DM Serif Display' (serif punch words). No Inter, Montserrat, Instrument Serif or Caveat. Every insert brief
+   must say so. Inter Tight 400-700 is the variable font in assets/fonts (declare 500/600/700 explicitly).
+5. **Coloured text is NEON / fluorescent with a glow:** accent neon lime `#C8FF00` (+ `GLOW` text-shadow), alerts
+   neon red `#FF2D55`, success neon green `#39FF88`. Never flat pastel colours (the old butter yellow is retired).
+6. **Animations go IN FRONT, in the lower band (chest / legs / table / board), and never cover the face.** This
+   is the layout the client approved (v2/v4 of the first reel). If an insert would reach the face (close-ups push
+   the chin down), make it smaller and lower it (scale .85, bottom still above y=1470) instead of moving it.
+   Captions then use the top band (above the head) or the chest band, whichever the insert leaves free. Placing an
+   animation BEHIND the speaker (`behind=True`, between base video and cutout) is available but only when the client
+   asks for it: she tried "everything behind" and preferred it in front.
+7. **CTA buttons and link/button labels ("Toca el link", "Agendar llamada", arrows pointing down) always go at the
+   BOTTOM of the frame, right above the y=1470 safe line, close to where the real Instagram link/caption is.** If
+   the face is down there (selfie framing), slide the button to the free side (bottom-left or bottom-right, it may
+   be scaled down to ~.6) instead of moving it up. The spoken line ("aquí te dejo el link") can stay as a caption.
+8. **Selfie framing:** when the face fills the lower half, the free wall is the TOP band: put inserts at y 225-565
+   and captions as one dark pill line right under them (`sm2` + `N()` neon word); the CTA rule above still wins.
+9b. **Type is BIG for the frame:** at 1080 wide, caption phrases >= 64px (700 weight), key words >= 130px,
+   full-screen card words >= 250px, CTA pill text >= 56px. If space is tight, shrink the insert (to ~.85), never the
+   type. The client flagged 46/100px as too small.
+9. **Audio level:** finish every render with `acompressor` + `loudnorm=I=-14:TP=-1.5` (Instagram loudness) when the
+   voice is quiet or uneven; never let SFX peak above the voice.
+10. **Punch-in zoom must not push the face into the insert or text zones:** after changing a zoom, re-run headpos.py
+   and re-check the snapshots.
+
+## Saved styles (named by the client)
+When the user says "edítalo con estilo <nombre>", read `references/styles/<nombre>.md` (and its reference JPGs)
+before Step 6 and build the captions, cards, grade and cutting from it; the house rules above still apply.
+To add a new style: download 1-3 reference reels (Apify `apify/instagram-scraper` with `directUrls` gives a
+`videoUrl`), study contact sheets + frame-by-frame crops, ask what she likes about it, and write a new file there.
+- `marca-personal-1`: fast conversational talking head; 1-3 lowercase words at a time with hard cuts, keyword stack
+  (small/BIG/small) with neon lime or neon red key words, white grid-paper interruption cards, B&W flips on
+  provocative lines, B-roll interrupts, cuts every 1-2s.
+- `video-viral`: cinematic POV/skit look; footage in a 1080x972 letterbox window on black, a permanent two-line
+  "POV: ..." hook title above it, dialogue subtitles coloured per speaker (white / neon), "Risas*" tags, B&W +
+  big emoji on the final punchline, few cuts, no inserts.
+- `marca-2`: premium "3 tips" list look; bottom fade to black, caption pair (white bloom sans + neon orange-gold
+  italic serif key word), glossy 3D orange number badges flying in per tip, full-screen icon cards hanging from a
+  light line, B&W close-up asides with plain subtitles, light leaks, 3D stickers on the CTA.
+- `marca-3`: clean agency/Apple-style explainer; talking head alternates with a white studio canvas (black S-curve
+  strokes) holding UI objects: the video shrinking into a phone mockup with social icons, dashed checklist pills with
+  X/check icons, tilted phone mockups with a connector to an icon; chest captions with neon lime key line, AR phone
+  cards by the desk, huge neon '"KEYWORD"' CTA.
+
